  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rajkumar Rathore vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 27 January, 2020 Author: Vishal Mishra Bench: Vishal Mishra 1 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh M.Cr.C. No.3463/2020 (Rajkumar Rahore vs. State of M.P.) Gwalior, Dated : 27.01.2020",
    "facts": "The applicant has filed this second application u/S 439, Cr.P.C. for grant of bail. The applicant has been arrested by Police Station Ambah, District Morena in connection with Crime No.380/2019 registered in relation to the offence punishable under Sections 420, 272, 273, 120-B of IPC and Section 51, 59 of Food Safety & Standards Act 2006. It is alleged by the counsel for the applicant that first application was dismissed as withdrawn with liberty to repeat the same after completion of investigation and filing of charge sheet. He is in custody since 28.11.2019. It is alleged that except offence under Section 420 of IPC all other offences are bailable in nature and offence under Section 420 of IPC is not made out in the fact and circumstances of the case.",
    "arguments": "Per contra, counsel for the respondent/State has opposed the bail application stating that one another case is pending against the present applicant for the offence under Sections 279, 337 of IPC, but he fairly submits that the aforesaid offence was registered in the year 1996.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Per contra, counsel for the respondent/State has opposed the bail application stating that one another case is pending against the present applicant for the offence under Sections 279, 337 of IPC, but he fairly submits that the aforesaid offence was registered in the year 1996.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
